# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and edit. Per-developer settings.
#
# Name of YOUR local code-signing certificate. A self-signed "Code Signing"
# certificate (Keychain Access > Certificate Assistant > Create a Certificate)
# has no Team ID, so macOS still re-prompts for keychain items after every
# rebuild (partition lists key on cdhash); install_local.sh then defaults dev
# installs to file custody. To use the keychain on a dev machine instead, create
# your own Apple Development certificate (it has a Team ID), put its name here,
# re-run ./install_local.sh, then run `ta credentials custody keychain`.
# See install_local.sh and CLAUDE.md.
#
# Leave unset to use the default name "Trusted Autonomy Local Dev".
# (macOS only today; Linux and Windows have no equivalent yet.)
TA_CODESIGN_IDENTITY="Trusted Autonomy Local Dev"
